		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: different radios...seperate BER on Pi-Star]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4998&amp;p=36393#p36393"><![CDATA[
I have an Anytone 878, TYT MD-UV390, Icom IC-7100 andID-50, and Yaesu FT5DR.  I use them all on the same HS and they all have different BERs.  I played around with calibrating the HS and have it down to where I get a BER of 0% on both Icoms, 0.1-0.3% on the Anytone and TYT, and 0.6% or below on the Yaesu.  You have to do some tweaking to find a good compromise.  I'm happy with under 1% and see no impact on it not being perfect with my systems.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5794">W3ATN</a> — Sun Mar 23, 2025 7:12 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
