		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4998&amp;p=36388#p36388"><![CDATA[
This is quite normal. <br><br>Most hotspots have a poor receiver that needs it's frequency to be fine tuned to match a particular radio. It is unlikely that a different radio will be on exactly the same frequency.  <br><br>It may be possible to adjust the frequency of your second radio using the OpenGD77 calibration function. You could use an SDR receiver with spectrum display to compare the two radios and make the necessary frequency adjustment. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Sun Mar 23, 2025 12:07 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
